<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23225" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infĭtĭātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infĭc-</span></b> ),
			ōnis,f.
		infitior, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a denial.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causam infitiatione defendere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 25, 105</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ipsam negationem infitiationemque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Part. 29, 102</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>a denying</i> or <i>disowning
				of a debt</i>, Sen. de Ira, 2, 9, 1: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circumscriptiones, furta, fraudes,
					infitiationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					47, 2, 69</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
